  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No famine drawn: an hourglass for the hard years, a rain cloud for «يغاث الناس» (both tafsirs: rain). Yusuf's words: no plate on him. STAGING v4: Yusuf's interpretation (48-49) is shown by its subject, the land of Egypt and its people (Al-Muyassar 48: its people eat the stores; 49: the people are given rain): gardens and farms with a plain group of three. No drop is on stage, so the camera stays wide (no close-up on a figure while Yusuf's words are recited). c1 (48): an hourglass for the seven hard years (no number drawn), the farms wither on 48:7 (both tafsirs: severe drought) and the people lower their heads; a wheat plate for the little kept back (48:13, Al-Muyassar: kept as seed). No cows, no eaten ears of grain, nobody hungry or hurt. c2 (49): a new year over the fields: rain falls on 49:8 (Al-Muyassar: given rain) with a rain-cloud plate, the people look up at it, and the fields turn green on 49:10 (abundant crops, As-Sa'di). Nothing is drawn for the pressing itself."
